## Why the whole system is non-commercial-only

This project orchestrates several external tools, each with its own
license, invoked as separate processes (never statically/dynamically
linked into this project's own code):

- **DeepMVP** (`bzhanglab/DeepMVP`, cloned separately by the user, never
  committed to this repo, gitignored): GPL-3.0. Invoked via subprocess
  (separate process, own CLI) -- not linked into this project's code, the
  standard basis on which independently-distributed GPL programs are
  invoked by non-GPL callers without extending GPL to the caller. This
  repo does not redistribute DeepMVP itself.
- **DeepPTMPred** (`kuikui-wang/DeepPTMPred`, cloned separately, gitignored):
  no LICENSE file in the repo, but the associated paper is CC BY-NC 4.0
  (Oxford University Press) and the corresponding author (Junwen Wang)
  confirmed directly by email (2026-07-29) that the code follows the same
  terms. Non-commercial only.
- **PyRosetta** (installed separately by the user, not part of this repo):
  RosettaCommons academic/non-commercial license. Non-commercial only.
- **MeToken** (`A4Bio/MeToken`, cloned separately, gitignored): MIT.
- **StackGlyEmbed**: lives in and is licensed by the sibling project
  `B-Cell-Epitope-Prediction`, reused here as an external resource, never
  vendored into this repo.

None of the above are distributed as part of this repository -- each is
cloned/installed independently by whoever sets up this pipeline, per
`README.md`. This LICENSE file covers only the code actually committed
here.

**This is not formal legal advice.** If you intend to use this pipeline
or its outputs beyond non-commercial research/academic purposes, verify
the current license terms of each dependency above directly.
